{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01 requires implementing a `solve(case)` function that:\n1. Takes a payload with `nodes` (a tree structure) and `required_symbols`\n2. Returns `removed_node_ids` and `retained_node_ids`\n\nLooking at the fixture data:\n- Each node has: `id`, `parent`, `symbol`, `depth`, `removable`, `utility`\n- `required_symbols` lists symbols that must be kept\n\nThe task seems to be about pruning a tree while keeping nodes whose symbols are required.\n\nLet me think about the logic:\n\n1. A node should be **retained** if:\n   - It is not removable (cannot be removed), OR\n   - Its symbol is in `required_symbols`\n   - OR it's an ancestor of a node that must be retained\n\n2. A node should be **removed** if:\n   - It is removable AND\n   - Its symbol is not required AND\n   - None of its descendants need to be kept\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Looking at the examples more carefully:\n\nFor case b-000:\n- Nodes with symbols in `required_symbols` = [\"root\", \"s1\"]: root, n1 (s1), n4 (s1)\n- Non-removable nodes: root, n1, n3, n5\n- Removable nodes: n2, n4, n6\n\nThe question is: what gets removed?\n\nLet me think about this differently. The task seems to be about keeping nodes whose symbols are required, and the tree structure means if you keep a node, you must keep its ancestors.\n\nA node can be removed if:\n1. It is removable\n2. AND it doesn't contribute any required symbols (either itself or through descendants)\n\nSo the algorithm would be:\n1. Mark nodes as \"needed\" if their symbol is in required_symbols\n2. Propagate \"needed\" upward - if a descendant is needed, all ancestors are needed\n3. Remove all removable nodes that are not needed\n\nWait, but non-removable nodes stay regardless. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually the logic might be:\n- A node is removed if: `removable=true` AND no descendant (including itself) with a required symbol exists in its subtree... but wait, non-removable nodes are always kept.\n\nHmm, let me think again. Maybe:\n- Remove a node if it's removable and its entire subtree (after removing other removable nodes) doesn't contain any required symbols OR non-removable nodes?\n\nActually, I think the simplest interpretation is:\n- A node is **retained** if:\n  - `removable = false`, OR\n  - Its symbol is in `required_symbols`, OR\n  - It has at least one descendant that is retained\n\n- A node is **removed** if it's removable AND has no retained descendants AND its own symbol is not in required_symbols\n\nLet me verify with case b-000:\n- `required_symbols` = [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n- root: removable=false → retained\n- n1: removable=false → retained\n- n2: removable=true, symbol=s2 (not required). Children: n4\n  - n4: removable=true, symbol=s1 (required!) → retained\n  - So n2 has a retained descendant → retained\n- n3: removable=false → retained\n- n4: removable=true, symbol=s1 (required) → retained\n- n5: removable=false → retained\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0 (not required). Children: none. → removed?\n\nWait, but if n6 has no children and its symbol isn't required, and it's removable, then it should be removed.\n\nSo for case b-000:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: [root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nLet me check case b-001 similarly:\n- Same structure, same required_symbols\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0, no children → removed\n- n4: removable=true, symbol=s1 (required) → retained\n- n2: removable=true, has retained child n4 → retained\n- Everything else non-removable → retained\n\nSame result: removed=[n6], retained=[root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nAnd case b-002:\n- Same structure, same required_symbols\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0, no children → removed\n- Same pattern\n\nSo the algorithm seems consistent:\n1. Start with all nodes\n2. A node is retained if: not removable, OR symbol in required_symbols, OR has a retained descendant\n3. Otherwise removed\n\nThis is basically: remove a node if it's removable, its symbol isn't required, and the entire subtree below it (considering only removable nodes that aren't required) would also be removed.\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. Build a tree (children map)\n2. Post-order traversal: compute whether each node's subtree has any \"must-keep\" content\n3. A node \"must be kept\" if: not removable, OR symbol in required_symbols, OR any child must be kept\n\nLet me code this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {node[\"id\"]: [] for node in nodes}\n    node_map = {node[\"id\"]: node for node in nodes}\n    \n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[node[\"parent\"]].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Post-order: determine if each node should be retained\n    retained = set()\n    \n    def should_retain(node_id):\n        node = node_map[node_id]\n        # Check children first\n        child_retained = any(should_retain(c) for c in children[node_id])\n        \n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            return True\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            return True\n        if child_retained:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            return True\n        return False\n    \n    # Find root(s) - nodes with no parent\n    roots = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"parent\"] is None]\n    for root in roots:\n        should_retain(root)\n    \n    retained_list = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"id\"] in retained]\n    removed_list = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"id\"] not in retained]\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_list,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_list\n    }\n```\n\nWait, there's a bug in my logic. `child_retained` uses `any()` which short-circuits, but the children that aren't visited won't be added to `retained`. Let me fix:\n\n```python\ndef should_retain(node_id):\n    node = node_map[node_id]\n    # Process all children first\n    any_child_retained = False\n    for c in children[node_id]:\n        if should_retain(c):\n            any_child_retained = True\n    \n    if not node[\"removable\"] or node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols or any_child_retained:\n        retained.add(node_id)\n        return True\n    return False\n```\n\nThis processes all children regardless. Let me write the final implementation.\n\nActually wait - I need to reconsider whether \"child_retained\" means ANY retained child, or whether children themselves need to be evaluated regardless of whether we short-circuit.\n\nThe issue: if we use `any()`, we stop processing children once we find one retained. But those unprocessed children still need to be evaluated and potentially added to `retained`. So I should process all children first.\n\nLet me write clean code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    node_map = {node[\"id\"]: node for node in nodes}\n    children = {node[\"id\"]: [] for node in nodes}\n    \n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[node[\"parent\"]].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    retained = set()\n    \n    def evaluate(node_id):\n        node = node_map[node_id]\n        child_results = [evaluate(c) for c in children[node_id]]\n        \n        keep = (\n            not node[\"removable\"]\n            or node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols\n            or any(child_results)\n        )\n        if keep:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n        return keep\n    \n    roots = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"parent\"] is None]\n    for root_id in roots:\n        evaluate(root_id)\n    \n    all_ids = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes]\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid not in retained],\n        \"retained_node_ids\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid in retained]\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me trace through case b-000 to verify:\n\nNodes:\n- root: removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: removable=false, symbol=s1, parent=root\n- n2: removable=true, symbol=s2, parent=root\n- n3: removable=false, symbol=s0, parent=root\n- n4: removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols = {\"root\", \"s1\"}\n\nchildren:\n- root: [n1, n2, n3]\n- n1: [n6]\n- n2: [n4]\n- n3: [n5]\n- n4: []\n- n5: []\n- n6: []\n\nevaluate(root):\n  evaluate(n1):\n    evaluate(n6):\n      child_results = []\n      keep = not True or \"s0\" in {\"root\",\"s1\"} or any([]) = False or False or False = False\n      return False\n    child_results = [False]\n    keep = not False (removable=false) = True\n    retained.add(n1)\n    return True\n  evaluate(n2):\n    evaluate(n4):\n      child_results = []\n      keep = not True or \"s1\" in {\"root\",\"s1\"} or any([]) = False or True or False = True\n      retained.add(n4)\n      return True\n    child_results = [True]\n    keep = not True or \"s2\" in ... or any([True]) = False or False or True = True\n    retained.add(n2)\n    return True\n  evaluate(n3):\n    evaluate(n5):\n      child_results = []\n      keep = not False (removable=false) = True\n      retained.add(n5)\n      return True\n    child_results = [True]\n    keep = not False = True\n    retained.add(n3)\n    return True\n  child_results = [True, True, True]\n  keep = not False = True\n  retained.add(root)\n  return True\n\nretained = {n1, n4, n2, n5, n3, root}\nremoved = {n6}\n\nSo:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"]\n- retained_node_ids: [\"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\"]\n\nThis makes sense! n6 has symbol s0 (not required), is removable, and has no children → removed.\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me format it as the required JSON output.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    node_map = {node[\\\"id\\\"]: node for node in nodes}\\n    children = {node[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for node in nodes}\\n\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[node[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    retained = set()\\n\\n    def evaluate(node_id):\\n        node = node_map[node_id]\\n        child_results = [evaluate(c) for c in children[node_id]]\\n        keep = (\\n            not node[\\\"removable\\\"]\\n            or node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols\\n            or any(child_results)\\n        )\\n        if keep:\\n            retained.add(node_id)\\n        return keep\\n\\n    roots = [n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is None]\\n    for root_id in roots:\\n        evaluate(root_id)\\n\\n    all_ids = [n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes]\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid not in retained],\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid in retained]\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01YnOpIgmaMeH9jm7xRxOeRC","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2195},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2195,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":85,"output_tokens":3091,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2753},"service_tier":"standard"}}